Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the React + Vite project

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` as a dependency in package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Integrated Analytics component
- Modified `src/main.jsx` to import and include the Analytics component
- Added `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'` at the top of the file
- Inserted `<Analytics />` component inside the React.StrictMode wrapper

### Files Modified:
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependency tree
- `frontend/src/main.jsx` - Added Analytics component to the React root

## Implementation Details:

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), 
I implemented the framework-specific instructions for React applications:

1. Used npm (the project's package manager) to install @vercel/analytics
2. Imported the Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/react'
3. Added the component to the root of the application in main.jsx, inside React.StrictMode

The Analytics component will automatically:
- Track page views and user interactions
- Send analytics data to Vercel's analytics service when deployed
- Work in development mode for testing (development events are not counted in production analytics)

## Verification:

✓ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✓ No breaking changes introduced
✓ Code follows existing project patterns and style
✓ Lockfile properly updated

## Next Steps:

After deploying this application to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Navigate to Analytics section in the dashboard to view data
3. Analytics data will start appearing after users visit the deployed site

Note: The ESLint configuration has a pre-existing issue unrelated to these changes. 
The build process works correctly and the added code is syntactically valid.
